WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.140
The Conjuring universe is poised to overtake
The Matrix as the most profitable R-rated

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.460
series of all time.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:11.630
How did the cinematic exploits of real-life
paranormal investigators Ed and Lorraine Warren

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:12.880
get so successful?

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.660
Let's get caught up before the return of fan-favorite
haunted doll Annabelle.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.880
After her first appearance in The Conjuring,
the Annabelle doll became a staple of the

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.500
Conjuring universe and even got two spin-off
films of her own.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:31.280
Starting with Annabelle in 2014 and continuing
with the prequel film Annabelle: Creation

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.220
in 2017, the spin-off series has been a modest
financial success.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.260
Though the first Annabelle received a relatively
cold reception from critics and audiences,

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.250
the film still grossed over $257 million worldwide.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.860
Annabelle: Creation performed much better
than its predecessor, grossing more than $306

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.860
million worldwide.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.560
It also was better received by critics and
audiences, which paved the way for yet another

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.560
Annabelle sequel: the upcoming Annabelle Comes
Home.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.620
While the previous Annabelle films have featured
scenarios separate from the rest of the Conjuring

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.060
universe, Annabelle Comes Home takes us back
to the Warren household.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.500
Married demonologists Ed and Lorraine Warren
keep a collection of artifacts recovered from

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.020
their supernatural cases in a locked room
inside of their home.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.800
This safe room is home to numerous haunted
items, including the Annabelle doll.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:26.920
In the Conjuring films, the Warrens' daughter,
Judy, is explicitly told to stay out of the

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.420
safe room.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.100
"You can't go into this room no matter what,
remember?"

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.120
"Yes, dad."

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:37.600
However, in Annabelle Comes Home, Judy's babysitter,
Daniela, shows a dangerous curiosity toward

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.180
the Warrens' artifact room.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.380
Having recently lost her father, Daniela is
obsessed with the afterlife, and, as a result,

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.440
she accidentally unleashes the evil spirits
kept within the Warrens' home.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.060
After the spirits are unleashed, Judy becomes
the primary target for the evil entities.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.900
Edward and Lorraine Warren, played by Patrick
Wilson and Vera Farmiga, are based on two

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.780
real-life paranormal investigators.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.740
The Warrens are famous for a multitude of
paranormal cases, including the Amityville

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.220
haunting, which spawned its own franchise
of horror films.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.900
The Conjuring is inspired by another of the
Warren's cases that took place at a Rhode

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.820
Island farmhouse in the '70s.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.520
The Warrens also founded the Warren Occult
Museum in Connecticut, which is home to a

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:27.820
variety of spooky and supposedly haunted artifacts,
including the real Annabelle doll.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:33.060
Though the Warrens are well known, the two
are considered controversial among skeptics.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:38.880
Neurologist Steven Novella, president of the
New England Skeptical Society, told USA Today:

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.280
"The Warrens are good at telling ghost stories.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.480
[...] You could do a lot of movies based on
the stories they have spun.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.400
But there's absolutely no reason to believe
there is any legitimacy to them."

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.940
Whether or not their work is legitimate, the
cultural impact of Ed and Lorraine Warren,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.640
particularly on horror films, is undeniable.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:02.200
Ed passed away in 2006, while Lorraine passed
away on April 18th, 2019.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.960
In the Conjuring films, the Warrens' artifact
room is shown to have numerous haunted objects

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.860
from the couple's previous cases.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:15.520
Throughout the series, the Warrens have advised
people in their house not to enter the room

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:20.300
or touch the objects, since the possibility
of freeing any of the spirits contained within

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.400
could be dangerous.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:26.320
Though we've only seen glimpses of all the
artifacts housed in the Warren house, Annabelle

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.700
Comes Home places a bigger importance on the
spirits in that room.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.160
Producer Peter Safran told Den of Geek:

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.120
"The idea of actually setting a film around
[the artifact room] was something that we

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.600
had in our mind for a while.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:42.760
[We] just thought that the third Annabelle
movie is the opportunity to really raise the

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.480
stakes."

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.620
Gary Dauberman, the director of Annabelle
Comes Home, is no stranger to the Conjuring

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.280
universe.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.550
Previously, Dauberman has served as a writer
for multiple films in the franchise, including

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.540
Annabelle, Annabelle Creation, and The Nun.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:02.739
Dauberman even got to go on location with
the crew as they shot The Nun in Romania - a

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.540
level of involvement not always guaranteed
for a screenwriter.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:11.160
In an interview with Collider, franchise producer
Peter Safran gave a blunt explanation as to

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.180
why Dauberman made the transition from writer
to director for Annabelle Comes Home:

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.880
"He got to a place, as a writer, where he
wanted people to stop f---ing up his movies."

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:26.440
Outside of his work on the Conjuring franchise,
Dauberman also worked on the 2017 adaptation

00:04:26.441 --> 00:04:32.020
of It and is slated as a writer for the upcoming
horror projects Are You Afraid of the Dark?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.020
and It: Chapter 2.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.620
In the Annabelle Comes Home trailer, a new
supernatural entity can be seen standing in

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.740
a corner of the Warrens' artifact room.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.300
After Daniela goes against the advice of Judy
and enters the room where all of the possessed

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.500
objects are kept, she hears the ghostly voice
of a woman:

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:49.980
"I like your doll."

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.960
That wedding dress belongs to the entity known
as the Bride.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:02.860
Early reports say that the Bride is a new
monster in the series that possesses women

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.200
who wear her dress and convinces them to kill
their husbands.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:11.360
After each woman is made to take out her new
spouse, the Bride goes ahead and kills her,

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:11.860
too.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.840
The introduction of a new demonic presence
could be a sign of films to come, especially

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:20.020
since previous spin-off films have been introduced
in a similar way.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:26.100
In both of the main Conjuring films, Lorraine
Warren has the ability to see and communicate

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.500
with ghosts and demons.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:32.440
In the first film, this ability is demonstrated
when she's able to see the evil spirit that's

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.640
haunting the Perron family.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.720
The Conjuring 2, meanwhile, begins with Lorraine
having a dark vision during a seance and communicating

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.940
with the demon terrorizing a family.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.340
Lorraine is also able to see the evil nun
entity throughout the film.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:51.160
In the trailer for Annabelle Comes Home, Judy
mentions that she can "see things" just like

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.140
her mother Lorraine.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:57.160
This implies that a prominent plot point in
Annabelle Comes Home will revolve around Judy's

00:05:57.169 --> 00:05:59.810
apparent ability to communicate with the evil
spirits.

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:05.260
A trend in the Conjuring universe is that
the sets for many of the films are allegedly

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:05.760
cursed.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:10.479
The unit publicist for Annabelle Comes Home
told PopSugar that ever since The Conjuring

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:15.199
2, all of the sets have been blessed by Catholic
priests prior to filming.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:19.860
"On The Conjuring 2, we had an exorcist that
was recommended to us by Lorraine [Warren]

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.220
- a friend of hers who's sanctioned by the
church to exorcise buildings but not people.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.300
Apparently there are different levels of sanctions
for exorcisms."

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.640
With all of the films in the Conjuring universe,
it can get a bit confusing trying to remember

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.260
how each story fits into the series' timeline.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.700
Annabelle Comes Home sits at an interesting
intersection in the timelines of both the

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.940
Annabelle spin-off series and the main Conjuring
films.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:48.380
Annabelle: Creation starts off in the year
1943, though the bulk of the film takes place

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:53.520
in 1955, with a group of young girls trying
to survive their encounter with the demon

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:54.840
inside the Annabelle doll.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:07:00.680
The original Annabelle takes place in 1967,
as a young couple try to protect their souls

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.920
from the evil intent of the doll with the
help of Father Perez.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:09.100
Annabelle Comes Home will take place in 1971,
but it's not the only film that takes place

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:09.940
during that year.

00:07:10.289 --> 00:07:13.900
The new film shares its setting with the original
Conjuring film.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:17.840
In the opening of The Conjuring, the Warrens
take the possessed doll into their custody

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.660
just before they leave for Connecticut.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:24.420
With the addition of Annabelle Comes Home,
the Conjuring universe has come full circle.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:30.020
On the screen, Ed Warren is a devoted demonologist
who works in tandem with his wife.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.960
However, Patrick Wilson, the actor who portrays
the late Ed Warren, started out far from the

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:38.220
tense atmospheres and spooky settings of horror
films.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:42.120
Wilson started his entertainment career by
playing leading men in different Broadway

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:46.380
musicals - and not only did he act, sing,
and dance on-stage, he excelled.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:51.880
In 2001, Wilson was nominated for the Tony
Award for the best actor in a musical, finding

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.660
himself listed alongside acting heavyweights
such as Kevin Chamberlin, Matthew Broderick,

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.440
and Nathan Lane.

00:07:57.729 --> 00:08:02.160
The following year, Wilson was the only member
of the previous year's nomination list to

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.520
return, though he ultimately lost to John
Lithgow.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:09.300
Aside from starring in musicals and playing
a demonologist on-screen, Wilson has a rather

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.720
diverse film portfolio.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:16.860
He appeared in the 2009 Zack Snyder film Watchmen
where he plays Nite Owl, a former superhero

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:21.500
reluctantly convinced to put his costume back
on after a spree of mysterious deaths.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:25.400
After getting to play a hero in Watchmen,
Wilson returned to the world of comic book

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.920
adaptations to play King Orm in the 2018 blockbuster
Aquaman.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:36.060
Vera Farmiga has had a successful career on
the stage, in film, and behind the camera.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.560
But the story of how she got here is certainly
unique, to say the least.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.600
Farmiga grew up in a small Ukrainian community
in Passaic, New Jersey.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:48.279
She discovered her love of performance after
auditioning for a high school stage production

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.780
and landing the principal role.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:54.060
From there, she became part of a semi-professional
Ukrainian dance group.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:59.820
After high school, Farmiga went to Syracuse
University to study acting, ultimately embarking

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:03.860
on a professional stage career, where she
was noticed by television and film producers.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:09.060
This attention led to roles in The Departed,
Down to the Bone, and The Manchurian Candidate.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.959
After appearing on-screen alongside the likes
of Meryl Streep, Heath Ledger, and Robert

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:18.140
De Niro, she was nominated for an Oscar in
2010, for her supporting role in Up in the

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:18.640
Air.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:25.680
Annabelle is a terrifying antagonist onscreen
— and the ostensibly true story behind the

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.380
real-life Annabelle doll is just as horrifying.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:32.940
Supposedly, the Annabelle doll was bought
by a woman for her daughter, Donna.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.999
Unfortunately, after Donna was given the doll,
she and her roommate started to notice some

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.860
strange occurrences around the house.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:44.500
A medium claimed that the doll hosted the
spirit of a young girl named Annabelle Higgins,

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.860
who was found dead where their apartment was
built.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:50.600
According to the medium, Annabelle wanted
to remain close to the girls.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.519
Feeling compassionate, the roommates gave
Annabelle's spirit permission to stay with

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:55.500
them in their apartment.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:10:00.600
However, after recurring bad dreams and suspicious
noises in the apartment, the Warrens stepped

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.100
in.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.780
"We are beyond terrified.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.320
We don’t know what’s going on, or what
to do.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.040
Can you help us?"

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:10.080
"Yes we can."

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:16.059
They told the girls that the Annabelle doll
was inhabited by a demonic entity, and the

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.900
doll was exorcised and given to the Warrens
for safekeeping.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:23.619
After Annabelle allegedly attempted to have
a priest killed, the Warrens moved it to their

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.400
Occult Museum.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:28.820
There, it remains a popular attraction for
tourists and supernatural enthusiasts.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:34.900
While pretty much every film in the Conjuring
universe has deep themes relating to Christianity,

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.180
the Annabelle films take a bit of a different
tack.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:41.839
They usually feature concepts regarding the
nature of motherhood, and the sacrifices that

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.660
parents have to make to protect their families.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:48.760
In Annabelle, Mia's willingness to sacrifice
herself shows how the best mothers are willing

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:51.800
to give everything to keep evil from corrupting
their children.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.580
Annabelle: Creation shows just how desperate
grief can make people.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.549
In their desperation to get their daughter
back, the Mullin family welcomes what appears

00:10:59.549 --> 00:11:02.480
to be the spirit of their dead daughter into
their house.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:07.620
However, the spirit is actually a demon that
goes on to terrorize the Mullins and the orphans

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.500
they'd taken in as a form of personal penance.

00:11:10.869 --> 00:11:15.580
With Annabelle Comes Home, audiences may see
some of these previously explored themes revisited.

00:11:15.589 --> 00:11:20.730
In The Conjuring, Lorraine is extremely concerned
with the well-being of her daughter Judy,

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.360
even seeing visions of her dead body floating
in a river.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:27.820
With Judy now targeted by Annabelle, it will
be up to Lorraine to protect her daughter

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:29.660
from the doll's evil influence.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.740
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:36.760
Plus, even more Looper videos about The Conjuring
universe are coming soon.

